    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a clear focus on exploiting favorable matchups, headlined by our strongest plays: **Christian Yelich** (74.33) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (72.03). **Christian Yelich** leads the charge against McGreevy, benefiting from a massive +13% boost due to dynamic platoon advantages and a favorable SP xERA of 4.54. Similarly, **Pete Crow-Armstrong** finds himself in an optimal leadoff spot against Kremer; while we acknowledge the strikeout risk inherent in the SP\u2019s skill set, the 16% park factor uplift and elite sprint speed potential make him a must-start as we hunt for scarce stolen bases. **Josh Smith** (64.66) also warrants attention, as Ure\u00f1a\u2019s slow delivery offers a high-probability environment for **Josh Smith** to swipe a bag, further bolstered by an 8% boost for occupying the #2 hole.\n\nOur decision-making process for the utility spots was narrow, with **Casey Schmitt** (43.03) serving as the most difficult omission. While **Casey Schmitt** offered a solid floor against Cease, his scoring was ultimately suppressed by the opposing pitcher\u2019s elite skill profile, which triggered a significant -19% penalty compared to the more opportunistic matchups facing **Luke Raley** (59.62) or **Carson Benge** (43.82). We remain cautious regarding **Yordan Alvarez** (60.44); despite his elite 0.475 xwOBA, the platoon disadvantage against Griffin creates a tighter margin than the raw talent suggests. As a reminder, **Trea Turner** remains sidelined, necessitating continued reliance on our middle infield depth to maintain our competitive edge in the 5x5 standings. Keep a close watch on **Dillon Dingler** (63.75), whose +14% platoon advantage against Springs is a primary driver for his inclusion over other bench options today.",
